      {
        "id": "v2-978ba-p65-practice-slot-5-slot-5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The koala population $P$ on an island satisfies $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=\\dfrac15P\\left(1-\\dfrac{P}{800}\\right)$, $P(0)=100$, with $t$ in years. Use $\\dfrac{800}{P(800-P)}=\\dfrac1P+\\dfrac1{800-P}$. Find $P(t)$ and $P(10)$, to the nearest whole koala.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(t)=\\dfrac{800}{1+7e^{-t/5}}$, $P(10)\\approx411$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dt}{dP}&=\\frac{5}{P\\left(1-\\frac{P}{800}\\right)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dP}&=\\frac{4000}{P(800-P)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dP}&=5\\left(\\frac1P+\\frac1{800-P}\\right)\\\\t&=5\\bigl(\\ln|P|-\\ln|800-P|\\bigr)+D\\\\\\frac{P}{800-P}&=Ae^{t/5}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(0)=100$: $A=\\dfrac{100}{700}=\\dfrac17$.\n$$\\begin{align*}7P&=(800-P)e^{t/5}\\\\P(7+e^{t/5})&=800e^{t/5}\\\\P(t)&=\\frac{800}{1+7e^{-t/5}}\\\\P(10)&=\\frac{800}{1+7e^{-2}}\\approx411\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-978ba-p65-practice-slot-5-slot-5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The mass $Q$ grams of a yeast culture satisfies $\\dfrac{dQ}{dt}=\\dfrac12Q\\left(1-\\dfrac{Q}{60}\\right)$, $Q(0)=5$, with $t$ in hours. Use $\\dfrac{60}{Q(60-Q)}=\\dfrac1Q+\\dfrac1{60-Q}$. Find $Q(t)$ and the time, to 1 decimal place, when $Q=30$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q(t)=\\dfrac{60}{1+11e^{-t/2}}$, and $Q=30$ when $t=2\\ln11\\approx4.8$ hours.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dt}{dQ}&=\\frac{2}{Q\\left(1-\\frac{Q}{60}\\right)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dQ}&=\\frac{120}{Q(60-Q)}\\\\\\frac{dt}{dQ}&=2\\left(\\frac1Q+\\frac1{60-Q}\\right)\\\\t&=2\\bigl(\\ln|Q|-\\ln|60-Q|\\bigr)+D\\\\\\frac{Q}{60-Q}&=Ae^{t/2}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $Q(0)=5$: $A=\\dfrac5{55}=\\dfrac1{11}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}11Q&=(60-Q)e^{t/2}\\\\Q(11+e^{t/2})&=60e^{t/2}\\\\Q(t)&=\\frac{60}{1+11e^{-t/2}}\\end{align*}$$\nSet $Q=30$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+11e^{-t/2}&=2\\\\e^{-t/2}&=\\frac1{11}\\\\t&=2\\ln11\\approx4.8\\text{ hours}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      }
    ]
